  "body": "### Summary\n\nFable's round 3 review on #1101 (LOT-100) returned APPROVE with four non-blocking findings. The PR used all three of its review rounds, so these are left to a follow-up.\n\n### Scope\n\n1. **Low.** While a poll is set, the composer shows `ComposerMessages.pollUnsupportedForm` for **every** `.unsupportedForm` (`ReplyComposerModel.send()`), including one that does not come from the poll check: an edit form of another message, a control `PostingBody` refuses. Fix: add a dedicated `PostingError` case for the poll-field check of `PostingFlow.pollFields`, match only that case, and test that a non-poll `unsupportedForm` with a poll set keeps the generic sentence.\n2. **Detail.** Add that case to `docs/lots/LOT-100-poll-creation.md` §Behaviour: the poll stays on screen, with its own sentence.\n3. **Detail.** `PollCreationTests.dateFields` checks the hour in Europe/Paris, so on a machine in that zone it cannot tell `device.timeZone` from `.current`. Use a zone build machines are unlikely to run in.\n4. **Detail.** `ReplyComposerModel`'s body is at 248 of the 250 lines `type_body_length` allows. Extract something before the next addition.\n\n### Sources\n\nThe round 3 verdict on #1101.\n\n### Blocked by\n\n#1101\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A non-poll `unsupportedForm` with a poll set shows the generic edit sentence, and a test covers it.\n- [ ] The spec describes the poll-field refusal at send.\n- [ ] The time-zone assertion fails if `closingCalendar` uses `.current`, whatever the zone of the machine running it.",
  "closed_by": null,
